# Target pin for the vLLM main matched build (docs/PLAN-MAIN.md).
# Wired to scripts/05-serve.sh main. Test util 0.8.
# Base: nvidia/cuda:13.3.1-cudnn-devel-ubuntu24.04
# Compile NCCL (sm_121) + PyTorch release/2.14 (12.1a) + vLLM main.
# Host may stay 13.0 + cuda-compat-13-3. Do not pip cu132 / NGC torch.
# Git heads + cutlass 4.7.0, not vLLM cuda.txt 0.6.17 / 4.6.2.
# Tagged deps: latest tagged as of 2026-09-19 except b12x (1.3.0 pins
# cutlass-dsl 4.6.2 vs image 4.7.0), triton (torch 2.14 ships 3.7.1),
# apache-tvm-ffi (tilelang 0.1.14 requires <0.1.13).
# Quality first: nvfp4_ds_mla 584 B DSV4 envelope, InstantTensor, no LMCache.
# Attention is B12X_MLA_SPARSE (b12x compressed MLA on the 584 B page).
# GPU util stays 0.8 (save option). Do not raise spark2 to 0.85.

HF_MODEL_ID=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731
HF_MODEL_REVISION=main
REQUIRED_ARCHITECTURE=DeepseekV4ForCausalLM
REQUIRED_MODEL_TYPE=deepseek_v4
REQUIRED_NAME_SUBSTRING=DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731

# Overridable so a differently tagged build of this same pin can be served without
# editing the pin: `IMAGE=vllm-spark-0731:main-030-0 scripts/05-serve.sh main-029`.
# The v0.30.0 base is built as :main-030-0. Earlier bases: :main-030-rc2
# (v0.30.0rc2), :main-030-rc1 (v0.30.0rc1), :main-029-proto2 (proto-v0.2.0),
# :main-029-1rc0 (v0.29.1rc0), :main-029-proto (proto-v0.1.0), :main-029
# (v0.29.0).
IMAGE="${IMAGE:-vllm-spark-0731:main-030-0}"
STACK=main
VLLM_RELEASE=main
VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm.git
# Lightweight tag `v0.30.0` on commit 9ed533eb4adf (2026-09-21T03:14:00Z), the
# latest upstream serving tag. One commit ahead of v0.30.0rc2
# (`fa6ff060667f`): #57554 `[Build] Fix DeepGEMM CUDA 12.9 release builds`,
# two files, build-only. Previous base: v0.30.0rc2 = fa6ff060667f, v0.30.0rc1 =
# a00a3544b93e, proto-v0.2.0 = f37c550bf635, v0.29.1rc0 = 7ee8a6dd0138,
# proto-v0.1.0 = 69db1c26b4, v0.29.0 = 98dff2a81.
VLLM_REF=9ed533eb4adfe48aef7e569a08daeccd2a773fed

B12X_VERSION=1.2.6
B12X_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x.git
# vLLM v0.29.0's b12x extra pins b12x==1.2.6. Correction 2026-09-13: the claim that
# "1.3.0 dropped the dsa_indexer names the SM12x overlays import" is true of b12x
# **master** (081b235931, 2026-09-12: only logits_paged / logits_contiguous remain) and
# FALSE of the 1.3.0 release, which exports all five (PagedDecodeMetadata,
# prepare_paged_metadata, uses_paged_schedule, plan_paged_schedule, logits_paged). So a
# bump is a build-path question, not a porting one: 1.3.0 has no git tag, and this build
# installs b12x from the source at B12X_REF, so either point B12X_REF at the release
# commit or install the release wheel (it is py3-none-any, no compilation) and record its
# hash for provenance. Pin the commit the working main-b12x image was built from (1.2.6).
# Identity of B12X_REF, verified 2026-09-13: this commit (2026-08-25T16:52:11Z) is the newest
# before PyPI published b12x 1.3.0 at 17:20:50Z that day, and its
# attention/dsa_indexer/__init__.py is byte-identical (sha256 f60e8f9d...) to the 1.3.0 wheel's.
# So this pin IS the 1.3.0 release state, and B12X_VERSION=1.2.6 is only what the tree's own
# pyproject declares (the release pipeline stamps the wheel version). There is no 1.3.0 git tag,
# and nothing to bump: the image already runs 1.3.0's code. Do not force B12X_VERSION to 1.3.0,
# which would put our metadata out of step with the installed package.
B12X_REF=3a437ab5168060e4d625f05e1625c04089f1ba37
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.7.0
QUACK_KERNELS_VERSION=0.6.5

CUDA_VERSION=13.3.1
FINAL_BASE_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:13.3.1-cudnn-devel-ubuntu24.04
BUILD_BASE_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:13.3.1-cudnn-devel-ubuntu24.04
TORCH_REPO=https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch.git
TORCH_REF=release/2.14
TORCH_VERSION=2.14.0
TORCHVISION_REPO=https://github.com/pytorch/vision.git
TORCHVISION_REF=release/0.29
TORCHVISION_VERSION=0.29.0
TORCHAUDIO_VERSION=none
TRITON_VERSION=3.7.1
# Held deliberately (bumped 2026-09-13 only the four above):
#   triton     3.8.0 exists but vLLM v0.29 pins triton itself; moving it alone risks the
#              kernel compilation vLLM does against its own pin.
#   nvdisasm   13.4.49 exists but is a different CUDA minor than this toolkit (13.3.1).
#   b12x       1.3.0 dropped the dsa_indexer names the SM12x overlays import, and measured
#              no faster than 1.2.6 on this pair. The reference engine uses b12x too, 0.15.3.
NCCL_REPO=https://github.com/NVIDIA/nccl.git
NCCL_VERSION=source
NCCL_NVCC_GENCODE="-gencode=arch=compute_121,code=sm_121"
PYTORCH_INDEX_URL=
TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=12.1a
# Overridable: the vLLM compile peaks well above 40 GiB at 16 jobs, which does not
# fit while the llama.cpp workload holds ~78 GiB on each node. earlyoom then kills
# the largest process, which is that workload, not this build.
#   MAX_JOBS=4 scripts/02-build-main-029.sh vllm-spark-0731:main-030-rc1-phase1
MAX_JOBS_TORCH="${MAX_JOBS_TORCH:-8}"
MAX_JOBS="${MAX_JOBS:-16}"
VLLM_ENABLE_CUDA_COMPATIBILITY=1
DG_JIT_USE_NVRTC=0
# DeepGEMM is not pinned here: vLLM's cmake FetchContent pins vllm-project/DeepGEMM
# itself (cmake/external_projects/deepgemm.cmake), and our own a6b593d checkout could
# not build this base (`activation_alpha=` and `third-party/deep_jit` exist only in
# the fork).
# ue8m0 is the scale column this checkpoint is served with and is exact; 0 forces a
# float32 SF that the fork refuses on arch 12 (csrc/apis/gemm.hpp:122). Forced here
# because configs/env.spark.sh still defaults the variable to 0 for the older stacks.
VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM_E8M0=1
DEEPEP_REPO=https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepEP.git
# Latest tagged: v1.2.1.
DEEPEP_REF=v1.2.1

FLASHINFER_REPO=https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer.git
# Latest tagged: v0.7.0rc3. Branch `main` is untagged HEAD.
FLASHINFER_REF=v0.7.0rc3
INSTANTTENSOR_REPO=https://github.com/scitix/InstantTensor.git
# Latest tagged: v0.2.0 (same as current main HEAD).
INSTANTTENSOR_REF=v0.2.0
FASTSAFETENSORS_REPO=https://github.com/foundation-model-stack/fastsafetensors.git
# Latest tagged: 0.4.0. Branch `main` is untagged HEAD.
FASTSAFETENSORS_REF=0.4.0
LMCACHE_REPO=https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache.git
# Latest tagged: v0.5.5. Branch `dev` is untagged HEAD. Unused at serve
# (no LMCache) but compiled into the image.
LMCACHE_REF=v0.5.5

TILELANG_VERSION=0.1.14
HUMMING_KERNELS_VERSION=0.1.15
# tilelang 0.1.13 and 0.1.14 both declare `apache-tvm-ffi<0.1.13,>=0.1.11`, so
# 0.1.12 is the highest usable version. 0.1.13.post3 installs but breaks tilelang at
# import: tvm_ffi raises "'tl.SwizzleMode' has no enum at string index 'NONE'".
# Previous base used this same 0.1.12.
APACHE_TVM_FFI_VERSION=0.1.12
# 0.2.9 requires apache-tvm-ffi==0.1.13.post3, which breaks tilelang.
# Stay on 0.2.8, the latest that works with tvm-ffi 0.1.12.
TOKENSPEED_MLA_VERSION=0.2.8
NVIDIA_CUDA_NVDISASM_VERSION=13.3.73

KV_CACHE_DTYPE="${KV_CACHE_DTYPE:-nvfp4_ds_mla}"
# MoE backend. Default humming from 2026-09-21 (round 105), was b12x.
# Two independent measurements favour it: `moehum-rc2` (b12x standing, 3
# passes) 58.1/102.2/132.3/152.9 sum 445.5, +6.7 %; `hum-k6-rc2b` (WO off,
# k=6, 5 passes) 58.5/111.6/146.8/160.6 sum **477.5** with both gates passing
# in all five passes and acceptance 53.1-64.3 %, +7.3 % over the immediately
# preceding default and +14.4 % / +13.7 % over the contract standing arm
# `proto2-030-rc2` (417.5 / 141.2). Against the same-day reference
# `refg-rc2b` (485.9 / 162.2) that leaves -1.7 % / -1.0 %.
# `MOE_BACKEND` is a launcher-side variable: it must be exported before
# `scripts/05-serve.sh`, or set here. Putting it in `SERVE_EXTRA_ENV` only
# sets the container env, the `--moe-backend` flag is already built by then.
MOE_BACKEND="${MOE_BACKEND:-humming}"
LINEAR_BACKEND="${LINEAR_BACKEND:-b12x}"
ATTENTION_BACKEND="${ATTENTION_BACKEND:-B12X_MLA_SPARSE}"
DRAFT_ATTENTION_BACKEND="${DRAFT_ATTENTION_BACKEND:-B12X_MLA_SPARSE}"
LOAD_FORMAT=instanttensor
INSTANTTENSOR_DRAFT_LOADER=auto

SPEC_METHOD=dspark
# Speculative depth. Default 6 from 2026-09-21 (round 104), was 5 here and 7
# in the arm protocol. Three measurements at k=6 are positive and all improve
# acceptance: `k6-rc2` (WO on) 55.9/107.6/132.2/149.9 sum 445.6, +6.7 % over
# standing; `wooff-k6-rc2` (3 passes) 56.9/102.2/137.5/151.8 sum 448.4;
# `wooff-k6-5-rc2` (5 passes) 56.3/103.7/132.9/152.3 sum 445.2, acceptance
# 57.5-67.5 % against 49.8-56.9 % at k=7, tokens per step floor held. One
# fewer draft pass per engine step, which is the only lever with a mechanism
# the profile supports.
NUM_SPECULATIVE_TOKENS="${NUM_SPECULATIVE_TOKENS:-6}"
DRAFT_SAMPLE_METHOD=probabilistic

BLOCK_SIZE="${BLOCK_SIZE:-256}"
TP_SIZE="${TP_SIZE:-2}"
NNODES="${NNODES:-2}"
PP_SIZE="${PP_SIZE:-1}"
SERVE_PORT="${SERVE_PORT:-8000}"
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION="${GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION:-0.8}"
MAX_MODEL_LEN="${MAX_MODEL_LEN:-65536}"
# Sized for the k sweep: capture must cover max_num_seqs * (k+1).
MAX_NUM_SEQS="${MAX_NUM_SEQS:-6}"
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS="${MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS:-12288}"
ENFORCE_EAGER="${ENFORCE_EAGER:-0}"
CUDAGRAPH_MODE="${CUDAGRAPH_MODE:-FULL_AND_PIECEWISE}"
MAX_CUDAGRAPH_CAPTURE_SIZE="${MAX_CUDAGRAPH_CAPTURE_SIZE:-36}"
LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=1024
SERVED_MODEL_NAME="deepseek-v4-flash dsv4"
TOKENIZER_MODE=deepseek_v4
REASONING_PARSER=deepseek_v4
TOOL_CALL_PARSER=deepseek_v4
ENABLE_PREFIX_CACHING=1

# Persist inductor/AOT between serves.
VLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE="${VLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE:-1}"
B12X_MLA_SM120_UNIFIED="${B12X_MLA_SM120_UNIFIED:-1}"
B12X_MOE_FORCE_A8="${B12X_MOE_FORCE_A8:-1}"
# WO projection overlay. Default off from 2026-09-21 (round 103).
# The c1 decode profile puts the o_proj region at 57.4 ms of a 150.6 ms step
# (38 %), and `nowo-rc2` measured the einsum path better than the overlay at
# every level (57.7 / 102.6 / 132.9 / 149.0, sum 442.2, spread 5.7 %, gates
# pass, acceptance 50.6-56.6 %, tokens per step 4.523-4.923) against the
# standing 51.7 / 98.0 / 126.6 / 141.2, sum 417.5. The overlay is a measured
# net loss, so it is no longer the served default. Set to 1 to restore it.
VLLM_USE_B12X_WO_PROJECTION="${VLLM_USE_B12X_WO_PROJECTION:-0}"
VLLM_USE_B12X_MHC="${VLLM_USE_B12X_MHC:-1}"
VLLM_USE_B12X_MOE="${VLLM_USE_B12X_MOE:-1}"
VLLM_USE_B12X_SPARSE_INDEXER="${VLLM_USE_B12X_SPARSE_INDEXER:-1}"
# Kept 2026-09-17 (round 45): the packed-indexer gather that materialises a full-cache copy on
# every layer of every decode step (~44 ms/step, named from a shapes trace as
# `aten::copy_ [17177, 64, 132]`, `64 x 132 = 8448` = the packed sidecar width). Reading the KV
# cache directly instead measured +27 % on the sum and +22 % at c6 across two identical runs
# (51.9/101.4/127.6/143.4 and 55.1/98.2/129.7/139.6 against 35.4/78.9/103.0/117.0), gates passing
# in every pass, with acceptance and tokens per step unchanged. See docs/EXPERIMENTS.md
# (`proto2-dgather`, `proto2-dgather2`).
VLLM_B12X_INDEXER_DIRECT_GATHER="${VLLM_B12X_INDEXER_DIRECT_GATHER:-1}"

# Phase 6: empty | lmcache | native. Default empty (quality pin has no offload).
# lmcache is the PLAN preference; native is OffloadingConnector FS if GDS/HMA fails.
KV_OFFLOAD="${KV_OFFLOAD:-}"
ENABLE_LMCACHE="${ENABLE_LMCACHE:-0}"

CONTAINER_NAME=vllm-ds4-0731
